llvm-3.7.1 patch: a weak-linkage structor is emitted as its own function (PS4)

This patch CHANGES CODE GENERATION for the complete constructor and
destructor (C1, D1) of a class whose structor has weak linkage for the
linker: an inline definition, an implicit or an explicit template
instantiation. Upstream 3.7.1 replaces such a D1 by the D2 (RAUW), so
the executable holds one body and no D1 symbol; the PS4 compiler that
built the game region kept clang 3.3's rule (CGCXX.cpp,
TryEmitDefinitionAsAlias: no alias to a linker-weak target, no
replacement): D1 is emitted as its own function that calls D2, which the
optimizer inlines when D2 is small and leaves as a tail jump when it is
not. A strong definition still becomes an alias. It is the 3.7.1 form of
tools/patches/llvm-4.0.0-structor-01-weak-structor-emitted.patch
(docs/DECISIONS.md D45: 507 strong aliases, 248 five-byte D1 thunks, 905
D1 bodies of their own over every vtable of the game region). Swept
alone over the game module, front end and code generation (round 270B,
5,496 rows): 53 functions appear that the pristine module does not hold,
2 change in bytes; the six rows that had no symbol are found (2 equal, 1
equal but for the thread-local access, 3 differ); no other row changes.

--- a/tools/clang/lib/CodeGen/ItaniumCXXABI.cpp
+++ b/tools/clang/lib/CodeGen/ItaniumCXXABI.cpp
@@ -3204,6 +3204,12 @@
   }
   llvm::GlobalValue::LinkageTypes Linkage = CGM.getFunctionLinkage(AliasDecl);
 
+  // PS4: a structor with weak linkage (inline, template instantiation) is
+  // emitted as its own function that calls the base variant, as clang 3.3
+  // emitted it; only a strong definition becomes an alias.
+  if (llvm::GlobalValue::isWeakForLinker(Linkage))
+    return StructorCodegen::Emit;
+
   if (llvm::GlobalValue::isDiscardableIfUnused(Linkage))
     return StructorCodegen::RAUW;
 
